ies with  small children walking by people walking  their dogs  go out for an evening run and it just  underscores the absolute surreal nature  of Life achieved these days as you have  these signs of normal life slowly  starting to return  made the you know the presence of War  being here is a great first step because  you're not sitting in a newsroom in DC  or New York and you are Googling your  stories  but you need to be here and you need to  you know you don't have to go run  through the trenches and put your life  on the line but talk to people go see  things with your own eyes have your  boots on the ground perspective that's  the best way to cut through the noise  and to tell the truth  [Music]  I lived in Paris for a few years when I  was younger  and I love living there because that's  where history happened when I moved to  Ukraine I had this overwhelming sense  that I'm where history is happening this  is it this is you know the most  important place in the world right now  this is the epicenter of Our Moment in  history our collective experience in  this life like we're living through  something that people will remember for  hundreds maybe even thousands of years  this is incredibly important historic  moment to be here and to experience this  it's incredibly gratifying because you  feel like you are have a front row seat  to  probably the most important story of our  lifetimes and even the last eight years  just to see how the incar the entire  country has changed so much I remember  spending a lot of time in mariopal over  the last eight and a half years when I  first got there in 2014 very Bleak kind  of post-soviet place  but the youth the young people who live  there the millennial generation  transformed that City  into this really bright promising place  [Music]  and I think that's such a tragedy then  that Russia went in and destroyed that  city  um and I think that what happened to  Mary Hoople is emblematic or  representative of what we don't 